  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights in Palestine (SRHR) 2021-2024</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights in Palestine (SRHR) 2021-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sverige har beslutat att arbeta mot en mer fokuserad ansats f&#xF6;r SRHR i Palestina. Denna ansats har resulterat i att Palestinian Medical Relief Society (PMRS) f&#xF6;resl&#xE5;s implementera ett tre&#xE5;rigt program med fokus p&#xE5; f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttrad service och &#xF6;kade r&#xE4;ttigheter vad g&#xE4;ller SRHR i Palestina. De SRHR relaterade behoven i Palestina &#xE4;r uppenbara och Sverige har ett merv&#xE4;rde inom detta omr&#xE5;de genom sitt engagemang och ledarskap inom omr&#xE5;den som kvinnors r&#xE4;tt till reproduktiv h&#xE4;lsa och m&#xF6;drav&#xE5;rd sedan 1960-talet, en erfarenhet som kan anv&#xE4;ndas f&#xF6;r att st&#xE4;rka SRHR i Palestina. SRHR utg&#xF6;r dessutom en del av Sveriges feministiska utrikespolitik vilket oms&#xE4;tts i handling i och med det f&#xF6;reslagna st&#xF6;det.

Det f&#xF6;reslagna st&#xF6;det &#xE4;r presenterat som ett program med en implementeringsperiod om 36 m&#xE5;nader med en total budget p&#xE5; 45 miljoner svenska kronor, som kommer att implementeras p&#xE5; V&#xE4;stbanken, i Gaza och i &#xF6;stra Jerusalem. Ut&#xF6;ver detta kommer 200 000 SEK att reserveras f&#xF6;r att genomf&#xF6;ra en granskning av intern styrning och kontroll av PMRS under avtalsperioden.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sweden has decided to work more towards a focused approach on SRHR in Palestine. This process has led Sweden proposing a program with the Palestinian Medical Relief Society (PMRS) to be implemented over three years, focusing on improving the SRHR services and rights in Palestine. The SRHR gaps and needs in Palestine are evident and Sweden has an added value in this areas as it has been a champion of women&apos;s access to reproductive and maternal health services since the 1960&apos;s and this experience can be utilized to strengthen SRHR in Palestine. Moreover, Sweden&apos;s feminist foreign policy, gives attention to SRHR and this shall be translated into programs and responses to on the ground. 

The proposed support is submitted in the frame of a program with an implementation period of 36 months with a total budget of 45 million Swedish kroner and will cover the West Bank, Gaza and East Jerusalem. This is in addition to SEK 200 000 to conduct an internal control review of PMRS to assess the organization&apos;s internal capacities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed program will be implemented by PMRS and will have the following goals:

1-  Palestinians, women &amp; men, girls and boys, without discrimination, have access to quality primary comprehensive health care focusing on SRHR and Mental Health and Psychosocial services (MHPSS) service and support delivery.

2- Mobilized and empowered local communities advocating for their SRHR rights with emphasis on youth, women and marginalized groups.

3- A resilient Palestinian civil society has been strengthened.</narrative>
  </description>
